/T (This momentum is supported by several factors: robust domestic consumption, sustained Gross Fixed Capital Formation \(Investment\) growth of 7.8%, and a strong push from Government Final Consumption Expenditure \(GFCE\), which surged by 9.7% in nominal terms, reflecting front-loaded fiscal spending on infrastructure. Sectorally, the tertiary \(services\) sector has been the primary engine, growing robustly at 9.3%, with the vital IT sector expanding at an even higher 10%. Furthermore, a healthy rebound in manufacturing at 7.7% and sustained construction growth at 7.6%, aided by policy incentives like the PLI scheme and public capex, demonstrates the broad-based nature of the recovery. )
